### Goal Model Summary

| Goal ID | Title | Text | Runtime | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|--------|-------|------|---------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G1 | Manage hospital room meal delivery and dish retrieval | Manage the delivery of meals and retrieval of dirty dishes in hospital rooms. | ; | Perform | - | Sequential execution as meals must be delivered before dishes are retrieved. |
| G2 | Deliver meal to inpatient room | Ensure food is delivered to the inpatient room. | - | Perform | AND | Both direct and tray-based delivery are essential. |
| G3 | Direct delivery | Deliver meal directly to the room table. | - | Achieve | OR | Either direct or tray-based delivery can fulfill meal delivery. |
| G4 | Tray-based delivery | Deliver meal on robot's tray, requiring potential cooperation. | - | Perform | OR | Either inpatient can retrieve or assistance is needed. |
| G5 | Check inpatient capability | Verify if inpatient can retrieve meal from tray. | - | Query | AND | Necessary before deciding on assistance. |
| G6 | Assist meal retrieval | Assist inpatient with meal retrieval if needed. | - | Perform | AND | Required if inpatient cannot retrieve alone. |
| G7 | Retrieve dirty dishes from room | Collect dirty dishes from the inpatient room. | - | Perform | AND | Essential part of the mission. |
| G8 | Unassisted dish retrieval | Retrieve dishes without human or robot assistance. | - | Achieve | OR | Either unassisted or with help can fulfill dish retrieval. |
| G9 | Assisted dish retrieval | Retrieve dishes with cooperation from another robot or human. | - | Perform | OR | Needed if unassisted retrieval fails. |

### Task Summary

| Task ID | Title | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|-------|------|----------|----------|------------------|---------------|
| AT1 | Place meal on table | Deliver meal directly to the room table. | AND | Hospital room | 1 | Single robot can handle direct delivery. |
| AT2 | Check tray retrieval capability | Verify if inpatient can retrieve meal. | AND | Hospital room | 1 | Single robot assesses capability. |
| AT3 | Assist meal retrieval | Help inpatient retrieve meal from tray. | AND | Hospital room | 2 | Two robots may be needed for assistance. |
| AT4 | Unassisted dish retrieval | Collect dishes without help. | AND | Hospital room | 1 | Single robot can handle if possible. |
| AT5 | Assisted dish retrieval | Retrieve dishes with another robot or human. | AND | Hospital room | 2 | Two robots may be required if unassisted fails. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G7 [AND]**
  - **Justification**: Both meal delivery and dish retrieval are necessary for the mission, hence sequential execution.

- **G2 -> G3, G4 [OR]**
  - **Justification**: Either direct or tray-based delivery can fulfill meal delivery.

- **G4 -> G5, G6 [AND]**
  - **Justification**: Must check capability and assist if needed.

- **G7 -> G8, G9 [OR]**
  - **Justification**: Either method can fulfill dish retrieval.

- **G3 -> AT1 [AND]**
  - **Justification**: Directly delivers the meal.

- **G4 -> AT2, AT3 [AND]**
  - **Justification**: Checks capability and assists if needed.

- **G8 -> AT4 [AND]**
  - **Justification**: Single robot handles unassisted retrieval.

- **G9 -> AT5 [AND]**
  - **Justification**: Two robots assist if unassisted fails.

This model ensures that the mission is executed efficiently, considering both possible methods for delivery and retrieval, and handling uncertainties through cooperation when necessary.
